1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,981
In September 2012, a nineteen-year-old
student at the University of North

2
00:00:04,981 --> 00:00:08,479
Carolina was found dead in
an apartment in Chapel Hill.

3
00:00:08,776 --> 00:00:12,888
On the bed near her, police found
a note, written on a fast-food bag.

4
00:00:13,626 --> 00:00:15,890
It said, "I'm not stupid."

5
00:00:16,368 --> 00:00:17,869
And then, "Jealous."

6
00:00:18,399 --> 00:00:20,864
Police believed her killer wrote it.

7
00:00:21,518 --> 00:00:24,087
Her name was Faith Hedgepeth.

8
00:00:24,506 --> 00:00:27,373
For nine years, no one was arrested.

9
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:32,857
Investigators had a man's DNA, and
hundreds of samples that didn't match.

10
00:00:33,330 --> 00:00:37,401
Then, in 2021, police
arrested a man from Durham.

11
00:00:37,818 --> 00:00:41,154
Investigators said his
DNA matched the scene.

12
00:00:41,612 --> 00:00:45,801
Now, fourteen years after she died,
he is on trial for her murder.

13
00:00:46,083 --> 00:00:48,245
He has pleaded not guilty.

14
00:00:48,583 --> 00:00:51,281
A prosecutor told the
jury, "The evidence in

15
00:00:51,281 --> 00:00:54,087
this case is louder than
the noise around it."

16
00:00:55,002 --> 00:00:59,438
His lawyer told them to ask something
else: "Where's the rest of the evidence?"

17
00:00:59,984 --> 00:01:02,117
The jury hasn't decided.

18
00:01:02,441 --> 00:01:06,054
This is what it has heard so
far, and what it won't hear.

19
00:01:06,492 --> 00:01:11,644
Faith Hedgepeth was nineteen,
a biology student at UNC Chapel Hill.

20
00:01:11,943 --> 00:01:15,133
She grew up in Warren
County, North Carolina.

21
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:19,751
She was a member of the Haliwa-Saponi
tribe, and a Gates Millennium Scholar.

22
00:01:20,202 --> 00:01:23,123
On campus, she sang
with an American Indian

23
00:01:23,123 --> 00:01:25,805
a cappella group called Unheard Voices.

24
00:01:26,609 --> 00:01:31,564
A friend told the jury she was goofy,
full of joy, and gave great hugs.

25
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:35,733
On the evening of the sixth of
September, 2012, police say,

26
00:01:35,733 --> 00:01:38,885
Faith and her roommate
studied at the campus library.

27
00:01:39,214 --> 00:01:43,468
After midnight, they went to a nightclub
in Chapel Hill called the Thrill.

28
00:01:43,793 --> 00:01:46,655
Video showed them leaving just after two.

29
00:01:46,986 --> 00:01:49,254
Police said that by three in the morning,

30
00:01:49,254 --> 00:01:51,619
the two women were back
at their apartment.

31
00:01:52,023 --> 00:01:56,099
That's the last time, police said,
Faith was known to be alive.

32
00:01:56,571 --> 00:02:00,210
At about half past four,
police said, the roommate left.

33
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:04,002
She came back around eleven
that morning, with a friend.

34
00:02:04,435 --> 00:02:07,419
They found Faith, and called nine one one.

35
00:02:07,906 --> 00:02:10,516
A medical examiner has told the jury that

36
00:02:10,516 --> 00:02:13,238
she died of blunt force
trauma to the head.

37
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:17,847
On the bed was a fast-food bag,
with a note written on it.

38
00:02:18,765 --> 00:02:21,539
Police released it two years later.

39
00:02:22,061 --> 00:02:24,377
It read: "I'm not stupid."

40
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:27,157
Then a word we won't repeat.

41
00:02:27,621 --> 00:02:29,011
Then, "Jealous."

42
00:02:29,542 --> 00:02:32,331
Police said they believed
the killer wrote it.

43
00:02:32,669 --> 00:02:37,197
Early on, police also said they didn't
believe this was a random crime.

44
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:41,832
In 2013, police and the
FBI released a profile.

45
00:02:42,147 --> 00:02:45,738
It said the killer might have
known Faith, and lived near her.

46
00:02:46,226 --> 00:02:50,028
Investigators had DNA from
the scene, from a man.

47
00:02:50,406 --> 00:02:53,271
They compared it with hundreds of samples.

48
00:02:53,642 --> 00:02:54,794
None matched.

49
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,805
Years went by.

50
00:02:57,311 --> 00:03:02,314
In 2020, a national TV special
was still calling it a mystery.

51
00:03:03,411 --> 00:03:08,662
On the sixteenth of September, 2021,
Chapel Hill police announced an arrest.

52
00:03:09,259 --> 00:03:13,285
Miguel Salguero-Olivares,
then twenty-eight, of Durham.

53
00:03:13,612 --> 00:03:17,151
Investigators said they found
him through genetic genealogy:

54
00:03:17,151 --> 00:03:20,314
the DNA from the scene led
them to distant relatives.

55
00:03:20,678 --> 00:03:23,901
North Carolina's attorney
general said a new

56
00:03:23,901 --> 00:03:26,930
DNA sample matched the profile from 2012.

57
00:03:27,763 --> 00:03:32,661
And police said he had not been a person
of interest early in the investigation.

58
00:03:33,361 --> 00:03:36,550
Faith's mother said
she cried tears of joy.

59
00:03:37,242 --> 00:03:40,200
He was charged with first-degree murder.

60
00:03:40,471 --> 00:03:45,075
Prosecutors later added rape,
burglary and sexual offense charges.

61
00:03:45,334 --> 00:03:48,347
The State is not seeking
the death penalty.

62
00:03:48,591 --> 00:03:51,704
He has pleaded not guilty to all charges.

63
00:03:52,103 --> 00:03:55,965
Before the trial, his defence
tried to have the case thrown out.

64
00:03:56,779 --> 00:04:02,004
A swab of a bloodstain from the bathroom
doorframe had been lost, and never tested.

65
00:04:02,643 --> 00:04:05,081
The judge called that "absurd."

66
00:04:05,535 --> 00:04:09,252
Prosecutors called it
negligence, not bad faith.

67
00:04:09,799 --> 00:04:11,623
And the case went ahead.

68
00:04:12,282 --> 00:04:16,617
The judge also ruled that the jury
won't hear about the genealogy that

69
00:04:16,617 --> 00:04:18,955
investigators said led them to him.

70
00:04:19,336 --> 00:04:23,959
Jury selection began on the
twenty-eighth of September, 2026.

71
00:04:24,210 --> 00:04:27,542
Twelve jurors and four
alternates were chosen.

72
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:32,365
In her opening, prosecutor Angela
Garcia-Lamarca told jurors his DNA was on

73
00:04:32,365 --> 00:04:35,698
the bottle the State calls
the weapon, and on the note.

74
00:04:36,175 --> 00:04:39,767
"This defendant was a
stranger to Faith," she said.

75
00:04:40,245 --> 00:04:44,678
"The fact that he was a stranger is
reason it took years to find him."

76
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:50,259
His lawyer, James Rainsford, told jurors a
statistical likelihood is not the same as

77
00:04:50,259 --> 00:04:53,821
a match, and that the DNA has
to be connected to the crime.

78
00:04:54,139 --> 00:04:57,560
The defence says his DNA wasn't
found on the neck of the bottle,

79
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,835
and that two bloody thumbprints
on it weren't matched to him.

80
00:05:01,742 --> 00:05:06,116
Faith's roommate, testifying for the
State, told the jury she had never known

81
00:05:06,116 --> 00:05:08,646
him, and never saw him in their apartment.

82
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:12,209
And a forensic technician
who worked the scene

83
00:05:12,209 --> 00:05:15,251
in 2012 admitted a mistake
with that bloodstain.

84
00:05:15,614 --> 00:05:18,095
"That step was missed," she said.

85
00:05:18,583 --> 00:05:21,996
Faith's parents have been
in court for the testimony.

86
00:05:22,850 --> 00:05:25,467
Her family says they
never knew the defendant,

87
00:05:25,467 --> 00:05:27,882
and knew of no link between him and Faith.

88
00:05:28,736 --> 00:05:33,993
So, here's where the case stands,
as of the thirteenth of October, 2026.

89
00:05:34,655 --> 00:05:39,151
Miguel Salguero-Olivares is on
trial for first-degree murder, rape,

90
00:05:39,151 --> 00:05:41,245
sexual offense and burglary.

91
00:05:41,734 --> 00:05:45,438
He has pleaded not guilty,
and he is presumed innocent.

92
00:05:46,186 --> 00:05:49,645
Prosecutors say the DNA
answers the question.

93
00:05:50,092 --> 00:05:53,026
His defence says it doesn't answer enough.

94
00:05:53,701 --> 00:05:58,505
Fourteen years after Faith Hedgepeth
died, a Durham jury will decide.
